Terms:
-------
Generations:
  Tock		: New uArch
  Tick 		: Process shrink of above Tock
  Optimization 	: Same uarch/process - optimization
  

Brand :
Each generation is split up into the following to target different markets
  		  Core 	  : i3, i5, i7, i9 with increasing perf/power
		  Xeon 	  : Server, lower clock, higher #cores, PCIe lanes
		  	    E (entry level), W (workstation : slightly higher), D (hyperscalers)
	  	  Celeron : Cheap PCs
	  	  Atom: Low power


Reference : https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Intel_CPU_microarchitectures

For e.g.,  Nehalem is the uArch, Westmere is the 32nm shrink and Westmere-EP is the 2socket Xeon processor


uArch List:
 Nehalem, Sandy Bridge, Haswell, Skylake and then the Coves start (cypress, Palm, Sunny, Willow Golden)

